```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "move a bag's bytes to its declared home; a plan unless approved"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.bag.homes"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.homes"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.homes"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.homes ~ the move that relocates bytes and re-anchors the declaration together

`home <bag> to=<home>` MOVES the bytes to a declared home and re-anchors the declaration together. It plans before it touches anything (the DRY-RUN default prints the plan and the command that performs it) and refuses an occupied destination rather than merging. `approve=true` performs the move, and no source-control verb ever runs: the bytes land in a working tree, and what enters a history stays the hand's own act. `repo=` names the registered repo id where the home reads repository.

The move relocates an operator's bytes across a boundary that matters (into a tracked history, or out of one), so it earns the explicit approval.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ plan-the-move · perform-it

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`plan-the-move` params=`bag/lares to/repository repo/lares-repo ~ print the plan and the command that performs it`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`perform-it` params=`bag/lares to/repository repo/lares-repo approve/true ~ move the bytes and re-anchor the declaration`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ bag · to · repo · approve

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug needs/required seat/1 as/<bag> ~ the bag to move`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`to` params=`takes/home needs/required ~ the home the bag moves to`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`repo` params=`takes/repo-id ~ a registered repo's id, where the home reads repository`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`approve` params=`~ perform the move; absent, only the plan prints`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/hand ~ the move relocates bytes across a boundary that matters; a plan runs unapproved, and the move itself asks approve=true`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ home-unknown · destination-occupied · repo-unregistered

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`home-unknown` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.homes bag/<bag> to/repository]] ~ to= expects one of the homes a bag may name`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`destination-occupied` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.homes bag/<bag> to/repository]] ~ the destination stands occupied; the plan names it, and nothing merges`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`repo-unregistered` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.registers]] ~ the repo id stands registered on no vessel here; register it first`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ planned · moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`planned` params=`exit/0 fields/[[bag planned from to why approved]] ~ the plan, with the command that performs it`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`moved` params=`exit/0 ~ the bytes moved and the declaration re-anchored inside the moved directory; a repository home names a working tree with nothing committed`>>
```

